---
import IndustryVisaPage from '../components/IndustryVisaPage.astro';
---
<IndustryVisaPage
  title="Visas for Film & TV Crews Filming Abroad | Unique Visa Services"
  description="Visas for UK film, TV and documentary crews filming overseas, including media and journalist visas, crew lists and equipment paperwork."
  crumb="Film and TV crews"
  h1="Visas for Film and TV Crews Filming Abroad"
  intro="Filming overseas often needs more than a standard visa. Many countries have special media or journalist visas, and some need filming permission before a visa is issued. We help production teams get every crew member cleared in time."
  who={[
    "Production companies and broadcasters filming overseas",
    "Documentary and factual crews",
    "Commercial and advertising shoots",
    "Freelance camera operators, sound recordists and producers",
  ]}
  visas={[
    ["Media or journalist visa", "Filming, reporting and documentary work in countries that have a specific media visa"],
    ["Business visa", "Recces, location scouting and production meetings, where the country allows it"],
    ["Work visa or permit", "Longer shoots or productions using local crew and facilities"],
  ]}
  sections={[
    { h: "Why filming trips need extra planning", p: [
      "Some countries will not issue a media visa until the production has filming permission from a government office or film commission. That can add weeks, so it pays to start early.",
      "Entering on a tourist visa to film can lead to equipment being held, footage being confiscated or crew being removed. We make sure everyone travels on the right visa for the job.",
    ]},
    { h: "Taking camera equipment abroad", p: [
      "Professional kit may need customs paperwork as well as visas. Many UK productions use an ATA Carnet, issued by UK chambers of commerce, to take equipment in and out of a country temporarily. We can point you in the right direction alongside the visas.",
    ]},
  ]}
  checklist={[
    "Passports for every crew member, with enough validity",
    "Crew list with names, roles and passport details",
    "Letter from the production company describing the project, dates and locations",
    "Filming permission or a letter from a local fixer or film commission, where needed",
    "Equipment list",
  ]}
  faqs={[
    { q: "Can my crew film on a tourist visa?", a: "Usually not. Many countries require a media or journalist visa for any filming for broadcast or commercial use. We check the rules for each destination." },
    { q: "How early should we apply?", a: "As early as possible. Where filming permission is needed first, the whole process can take several weeks." },
    { q: "Can you handle a whole crew at once?", a: "Yes. Send us the crew list and travel dates and we'll manage every application together." },
  ]}
  related={[["Performers and touring visas", "/performers-touring-visas/"], ["Trade fair and exhibition visas", "/trade-fair-exhibition-visas/"]]}
/>
